# Conformance probe pack for items by kind (spec 0.8), most significant bit
# first. Public. The message has no kinds; each item of recs selects one.
#
#   byte 0      n
#   byte 1      the number of recs
#   each rec    [x : 4][kind code : 4], then by kind
#     point  1    y in 8 bits
#     alt    3    y in 16 bits
#     text   2    an 8-bit length in bytes, then a two-character label
#     empty  0    nothing
#
# `point` and `alt` require the same key: an item decoded as `alt` is written
# as `alt` again because it records its kind; an item from another format
# with y is written as `point`, the first kind whose `requires` it satisfies.
format     conformance-seq-kinds
version    0.8.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
layout     sequential
bit_order  msb
field   probe.n  8  uint
group   probe.recs count 8
  field  probe.x  4  uint
  kind   point
  when   4  1
  requires probe.y
  field  probe.y  8  uint
  kind   alt
  when   4  3
  requires probe.y
  field  probe.y  16  uint
  kind   text
  when   4  2
  requires probe.label
  length 8
    field  probe.label  16  ascii
  end
  kind   empty
  when   4  0
end
